Chapter: DecimalScaleGuard
  cites Foreword chapter Decimal

 Track D item 19, the Decimal leg. 10^18 is the largest power of ten that fits
 a signed 64-bit integer. 10^19 wraps negative, and 10^64 is EXACTLY ZERO,
 because 10^n is 2^n times 5^n and the low 64 bits lose every factor of two
 once n reaches 64. dec-pow10 is a divisor in dec-to-text, dec-whole-part,
 dec-frac-part, dec-div, dec-round and dec-truncate.

 Guarded because something runs it (red's ruling, extended to this leg
 2026-08-16): codex/test/lib/decimal-test.codex. That test never calls
 dec-from-text at all, so the parser had no runner of any kind.

 Measured on the unguarded chapter: a fraction of 64 digits parses cleanly to
 dec-scale 64, and dec-to-text on the result dies !EXC=00, a DIVIDE error
 rather than the !EXC=06 the rest of this campaign produces.

 The scale is not only the parser's to set. dec-mul ADDS the two scales, so two
 scale-32 values reach 64 by arithmetic, and dec-new takes a scale from its
 caller directly. Guarding the parser alone would have closed one of three
 doors (L-CAPABILITY), so the saturation sits in dec-pow10 where every consumer
 must pass, and the two producers clamp as well so the scale they report is the
 scale they actually carry.

 Row 8 is the discriminator: eighteen digits is the largest scale that is fully
 representable and must survive unclamped, so a guard that saturated lower
 would pass every hostile row and fail there.

Section: Inputs

 Sixty-four fraction digits, which is where dec-pow10 reaches zero.

  d64 : Text = "1.1234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234"

 Twenty, which is past the representable limit but short of the zero divisor:
 unguarded this parsed to scale 20 and dec-pow10 20 is a WRAPPED NEGATIVE, so
 the arithmetic was wrong without ever faulting.

  d20 : Text = "1.12345678901234567890"

 Exactly eighteen. Legitimate, and must not move.

  d18 : Text = "1.123456789012345678"

Section: Helpers

  parse-row : Text, Text -> Text
  parse-row (label) (s) =
    let d = dec-from-text s 2
    in label & " scale=" & show (d.dec-scale) & " text=" & dec-to-text d

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (parse-row "1-plain" "1.5")
    print-line-uni ("2-round " & dec-to-text (dec-round (dec-from-parts 3 456 3) 1))
    print-line-uni ("3-mul-small scale=" & show ((dec-mul (dec-new 150 2) (dec-new 200 2)).dec-scale) & " text=" & dec-to-text (dec-mul (dec-new 150 2) (dec-new 200 2)))
    print-line-uni (parse-row "4-frac64" d64)
    print-line-uni (parse-row "5-frac20" d20)
    print-line-uni ("6-new-scale64 text=" & dec-to-text (dec-new 1 64))
    print-line-uni ("7-mul-scale32 scale=" & show ((dec-mul (dec-new 1 32) (dec-new 1 32)).dec-scale))
    print-line-uni (parse-row "8-frac18" d18)
  end

